{"id":"G3870","lemma":"παρακαλέω","transliteration":"parakaleō","sayIt":"parakaleō","language":"Greek","partOfSpeech":"verb","gloss":"to plead/comfort","meaning":"παρακαλέω, -ῶ,\n[in LXX chiefly for נחם ni., pi. ;]\n1. to call to one, call for, summon: Act.28:20 (R, mg.; R, txt., entreat); hence (of the gods: Dem., Xen., al.), to invoke, call on, beseech, entreat: τ. πατέρα μου, Mat.26:53; τ. κύριον, 2Co.12:8; in late writers (Polyb., Diod., al.; rarely in LXX; in π., see Deiss., LAE, 176.14), also of men: absol., Phm 9; with accusative, Mat.8:5, Mrk.1:40, Act.16:9, al.; with inf., Mrk.5:17, Luk.8:41, Act.8:31, al.; before ἵνα (see M, Pr., 205, 208), Mt 14\"36, Mrk.5:18, Luk.8:31, al.\n2. to admonish, exhort: absol., Luk.3:18, Rom.12:8, 2Ti.4:2, al.; with accusative, Act.15:32, 1Th.2:11, Heb.3:13, al.; id. before inf., Act.11:23, Rom.12:1, Php.4:2, 1Th.4:10, al.; before ἵνα (see M, Pr., l.with), 1Co.1:10, 2Co.8:6, 1Th.4:1, al.\n3. to cheer, encourage, comfort (Plut., LXX: Jb 43, Isa.35:3, Sir.43:24, al.): with accusative, 2Co.1:6, Eph.6:22, Col.2:2, al.; id. before ἐν, 1Th.4:18; διά, 2Co.1:4; pass., Mat.5:4, Luk.16:25, Act.20:12.\nSYN.: παραμυθέω (cf. M, Th., 25). (AS)","glosses":["urge","begged","encourage","pleaded with","urged","comforted"],"count":104,"occurrences":[{"chapterId":"mat-2","v":18,"renderings":{"bsb":"to be comforted","kjv":"be comforted"}},{"chapterId":"mat-5","v":4,"renderings":{"bsb":"will be comforted"}},{"chapterId":"mat-8","v":5,"renderings":{"bsb":"and pleaded","kjv":"beseeching"}},{"chapterId":"mat-8","v":31,"renderings":{"bsb":"begged","kjv":"besought"}},{"chapterId":"mat-8","v":34,"renderings":{"bsb":"they begged Him","kjv":"they besought"}},{"chapterId":"mat-14","v":36,"renderings":{"bsb":"begged","kjv":"besought"}},{"chapterId":"mat-18","v":29,"renderings":{"bsb":"and begged","kjv":"and besought"}},{"chapterId":"mat-18","v":32,"renderings":{"bsb":"you begged","kjv":"thou desiredst"}},{"chapterId":"mat-26","v":53,"renderings":{"bsb":"call